For the information of members, the variation to what was on the Notice Paper is to make sure that digital duty of care is dealt with today, rather than the tax measures. Originally we had planned to deal with the tax measures today, but that was on the basis of early planning that they would have been introduced yesterday. This is to avoid a circumstance where we're asking the House to vote on tax legislation on the same day in which it is introduced. It's a very long amendment, which is why I've had it circulated. But that's the substance of the change. 

