Senator COLLINS (New South Wales) (11:24): I move: 

I move that the Senate: 

(a) notes that: 

i. in February 2026 the Albanese Labor Government announced plans to divest historic and operationally significant Defence sites, including Victoria Barracks Sydney, at market value; 

ii. on 8 November 2026, following widespread opposition from veterans, serving personnel and the community, the Government announced that Victoria Barracks Sydney would remain in public ownership, but confirmed that Defence personnel would continue to be evicted from the site; 

iii. despite retaining the site in public ownership, the Government intends to transfer Victoria Barracks Sydney out of the Defence estate, with all but a handful of Defence personnel expected to be evicted by the end of 2026; 

iv. Victoria Barracks Sydney has been an Army barracks for more than 180 years and remains an operational Defence facility pending the planned relocation of personnel; and 

v. the Senate Foreign Affairs, Defence and Trade References Committee's interim report of 16 September 2026 recommended an immediate halt to the Defence estate divestment program; 

(b) calls on the Albanese Labor Government to: 

i. immediately cease the eviction of Defence personnel from Victoria Barracks Sydney; 

ii. guarantee that Victoria Barracks Sydney remains an operational military facility within the Defence estate, rather than merely retaining the site in public ownership; 

iii. immediately halt the Defence estate divestment program, consistent with the Senate committee's recommendation; and 

iv. protect other historic and strategically significant Defence sites, including Lancer Barracks, Parramatta, Stony Head Training Area, Tasmania and Irwin Barracks, Perth, and preserve their capacity for current and future Defence use; 

(c) condemns the Albanese Labor Government for proceeding with the removal of Defence personnel from Victoria Barracks Sydney in the lead up to Christmas despite its decision to retain the site in public ownership and the continuing opposition of veterans, serving personnel and the community; 

(d) calls on the Albanese Labor Government to release the 'independent audit of the Defence estate' as provided to the Government in December 2023; and 

(e) directs that this resolution be communicated by message to the House of Representatives. 

