Senator SHOEBRIDGE (New South Wales—Leader of the Australian Greens) (12:06): There is a complete lack of engagement from this government with the issues raised by the INSLM. I quoted the INSLM and I will correct the INSLM on one thing. It's Philip K Dick, not Philip J Dick. I quoted the INSLM directly because there was that clear sense of just utter frustration coming from the most senior person appointed at a Commonwealth level to oversight these laws, who's seen every time one of these laws has been tried and who's seen the evidence that we don't get to see, because the Independent National Security Legislation Monitor can see the affidavits, the secret affidavits and the police reports. The INSLM has actually gone behind and seen more than I've seen. It's seen more than the minister's seen. It's seen more than any member of this parliament has seen, and it's seen the way these things work and has said: 'Stop doing these things. They don't work. They degrade our civil society.' For the government to just dismiss them, to not even engage with them and to bury the report shows just how little regard Labor and their mates in the coalition and their cheer squad in One Nation have for basic rights and civil liberties. 

