Legal and Constitutional Affairs References Committee 

Reference 

Senator LAMBIE (Tasmania) (15:54): I move: 

That the following matter be referred to the Legal and Constitutional Affairs References Committee for inquiry and report by 1 March 2027: 

The establishment of an Australian Federal Police (AFP) Blue Card scheme to provide accessible medical and psychological treatment to current and former AFP members, with particular reference to: 

(a) the adequacy of existing legislative, compensation, support, treatment and rehabilitation arrangements, including the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988, in addressing the occupational health risks and accepted service-related injuries and diseases experienced by AFP members; 

(b) consideration of previous reviews relevant to the impact of AFP service on members; 

(c) the design, scope and eligibility criteria of a proposed AFP Blue Card, including appropriate coverage for current and former members, and recognition of the different operational exposures and cumulative health impacts associated with employment in federal policing, and the potential for non-liability access to medical and psychological treatment; 

(d) the application of comparable healthcare models, particularly the Department of Veterans' Affairs White Card scheme, including treatment entitlements, provider arrangements and fee schedules; 

(e) the legislative and regulatory reforms required to establish an AFP Blue Card scheme, including funding and implementation considerations; 

(f) the intended objectives of an AFP Blue Card scheme such as improving member health and wellbeing and supporting retention of experienced operational personnel within the AFP to improve operational capacity; and 

(g) any other related matters. 

Senator O'SULLIVAN (Western Australia—Deputy Manager of Opposition Business in the Senate) (15:54): I seek leave to make a short statement. 

The DEPUTY PRESIDENT: Leave is granted to make a short statement of one minute. 

Senator O'SULLIVAN: The coalition has long supported measures to improve the health and wellbeing of Australian Federal Police personnel, including through better access to treatment and rehabilitation. That included our 2025 commitment to pursue a police blue card scheme in government if we had won that year's election. We believe that this kind of scheme continues to invite serious consideration, including in respect of its potential benefits for serving and former AFP members, as well as issues around how it could best be implemented and financially supported. Therefore, we support the proposed inquiry. 

Question agreed to.

